YuVi Glow — License
====================

This file has two parts: a preamble stating the values behind this project
(not itself a software license — no copyright grant, no permissions, no
warranty terms), followed by the actual operative license, the GNU Affero
General Public License version 3 (AGPL-3.0).

See plan/issues/17-project-licensing.md in this repository for why AGPL-3.0 was
chosen (short version: this project depends on JUCE, which requires either
AGPL-3.0 or a paid commercial JUCE license — AGPL-3.0 is the fully
free/open-source path). See CREDITS.md for attribution of every third-party
work used in this project.


PREAMBLE
--------

The values below are adapted from CHAOS_Control.lic by Robert Lee Coffman
(also known as YuVi / Cache Refresh), source:
https://github.com/cacherefresh/LICENSES

This project is built and shared in that spirit:

  Rights to life, liberty, and the pursuit of happiness are treated as
  inherent, not granted by permission. That same spirit of good faith
  extends to how this software is offered to others: freely, for anyone
  to use, study, modify, and share.

  Kindness is the only real currency. Character, then competence, in that
  order. Resources — including the effort behind this project — are meant
  to advance shared understanding and capability, not to be hoarded.

  Progress should not come at the risk of the people it's meant to serve.
  Build things that are tested, that have a backup plan, and that learn
  from what came before rather than repeating avoidable mistakes.

  Credit is given, deliberately and specifically, to everyone whose work
  this project builds on — see CREDITS.md.

This preamble does not modify, restrict, or expand the legal terms of the
AGPL-3.0 license below. It is a statement of intent, not a license grant.


